+
+
+    
+    OUTLAW CITY: 10-minute playtest (owner, no dev tools)
+
+    Play like a new player. Don't open the F8 dev panel and don't run any commands. Use Studio Play (place 132163592957463) or a phone. Write one short line per step: what happened and how it felt. Studio's Output prints [Milestone] ... FirstCar / FirstRobbery / FirstEscape ... s after join; copy those three lines too.
+
+    #
+Minutes
+Do this
+Note down
+1
+0:00
+Join and read the tip on the left.
+Did you know what to do? Did the tip get in the way?
+2
+0:30
+Get a car (the Spawn Car button, or V on PC).
+How many clicks or taps? Were you seated?
+3
+1:00
+Drive to the 24/7 MART using the floating marker.
+Easy to find? Did the markers clutter the screen?
+4
+2:00
+Rob the register: hold E, or tap the prompt on a phone. Stay inside for the countdown.
+Was it clear what to do and how long to wait?
+5
+2:30
+Get back in your car and try to lose the police.
+Did "break line of sight, stay hidden" make sense? Did you escape? Fair, too easy or too hard?
+6
+4:00
+If you were caught: sit out the jail time and look at the store marker's "Reopens in" timer.
+Did jail or the wait make you want to stop?
+7
+5:30
+While driving, press Spawn Car again (with 2 cars, pick the other one in the garage).
+Were you seated in the new car, able to drive right away, with the camera behind the car?
+8
+6:30
+Drive to OUTLAW MOTORS, walk to the desk, open the window.
+Does the Muscle at $15,000 feel worth working for? Is the "robberies left" line clear?
+9
+8:00
+Rob again and try a different escape route.
+Better or worse than the first time?
+10
+9:30
+Leave and rejoin.
+Is your cash the same as when you left?
+
+    On a phone, also note: - Can you read the robbery panel, the tip and the markers? - Do they cover the driving buttons or the thumbstick?
+
+    Send back: the three [Milestone] lines, one line per step, and your call on: - the 90 s store reopen after a failed robbery; - the $15,000 Muscle price.
+
+    
+    
+      
+        
+                
+        
+        
+              
+      
+    
+  
+
